From b4d227c070c5480e382712489dd7e4a1840bbdbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:04:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Energy and water budget meter (instrumentation)

config_energy_meter (&nhyd_model, .false.): per-step global dry mass,
water and total energy at six points of atm_srk3, written as EB lines on
rank 0's stderr. E = IE + PE + KE + LV0*Wv - LF0*(Wi + Pice) (+ g z_sfc P)
in the energy the dynamics integrates: IE = cv T_m from MPAS's EOS,
(1+qt) loading on PE and KE, liquid water as the zero. Every global sum
is an order-independent fixed-point sum (6 int64 digits of base 2^40,
after MOM6's reproducing_sum); the precipitation totals and the run's
reference energy are carried in the restart file.

Test switches for the meter, microphysics off only:
config_energy_test_heating / _cooling (W/m2, 0 = off) apply a prescribed
8-h heat source and low-level sink, energy-consistently (dE = q);
config_energy_test_dry zeroes the moist species at the first step.

The meter only reads the state: with it on or off the forecast is
bit-identical to the previous commit.

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
